{
  "rule_id": "R29_131",
  "target": "ts",
  "tier": "T3",
  "governed_construct": "A diagnostic-output site: each call of a method on a value of the runtime's built-in Console type (the global `console`, reached directly, via globalThis, or through any alias/parameter typed Console), and each `debugger` statement.",
  "interpretation": "The rule forbids leftover debugging output. A call on the built-in Console object conforms only when it is legitimate error/warning reporting: `console.error` and `console.warn`. Every other Console method (log, debug, info, trace, dir, table, time/timeEnd/timeLog, count, group) is debug code and violates, as does any `debugger` statement. Whether a receiver is the built-in console is decided by binding and type, not by spelling: a parameter typed `Console` that is passed `console` is the built-in console, so `sink.log(...)` violates; a local parameter named `console` whose type is an application-defined interface (e.g. an in-game console UI) is not the built-in Console, so its `.log` calls are neither instances nor violations. Calls to application loggers (e.g. an imported `logger.info`) are not instances. A file with no Console calls and no debugger statements is NOT_APPLICABLE; a file whose only instances are console.error/console.warn is SATISFIED.",
  "fixtures": [
    {
      "id": "pos_01",
      "set": "dev",
      "kind": "positive",
      "file": "dev/pos_01.ts",
      "expected": "SATISFIED"
    },
    {
